# Throwaway scripts run against a live database — seeding a branch, planting a
# sign-in code to drive a flow by hand. They are written next to the workspace
# they import from, which is how one of them got committed by a `git add -A`.
# Named rather than tidied up by hand, because the tidying is the step that
# gets skipped.
probe.mts
plant.mts
seed.mts
reseed.mts
cleanup.mts

# Unpacked from the design bundle beside it; the zip is the artefact.
design/unpacked/

# Written by `vercel link` at the repo root: an OIDC token, not configuration.
# Narrower than the `.env*` the CLI adds, which would also swallow the
# `.env.example` files that are the documentation of what each app needs.
/.env.local

# iOS signing material, minted against the App Store Connect API key.
# A distribution private key and the profile it is embedded in; `credentials.json`
# holds the .p12 password in clear. None of it belongs in a repository, and the
# certificate can be reissued from Apple if lost — see `apps/mobile/README.md`.
apps/mobile/credentials.json
apps/mobile/credentials/

# Written by `vercel integration add neon`, which installs the provider's agent
# skills into the repo as a side effect of provisioning a database. Useful to
# have on a machine, not something this repository is asserting: they are a
# vendor's documentation, versioned by a lockfile nothing here reads, and they
# arrived unasked alongside a connection string.
.agents/
skills-lock.json
# And the symlinks it leaves under `.claude/skills` pointing into `.agents`,
# which would otherwise be committed as dangling links on any other machine.
.claude/skills/

# Claude Code's per-machine settings. `.local.json` is the half that is not
# meant to be shared — it accumulates one developer's approved commands, with
# absolute paths out of their own scratch directory.
.claude/settings.local.json
